    "details": {
      "alignment": "Lawful Good",
      "type": {
        "value": "humanoid",
        "subtype": "koopa"
      },
      "cr": 3,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Era sheet: 18 Harvestide, 1035 BF, Bowser's Castle.</em> Art and stats describe this figure on the night the castle came down (events.json <code>bowser_throne_room_compromise</code> and <code>the_assault_on_bowsers_castle</code>), not the present day of the campaign (1040 BF).</p><p><strong>Session kit — The Castle Comes Down (Session III).</strong> A GM kit for the night after the breach, not a filed event; nothing on this sheet changes the canon record. The run-sheet is <code>docs/sessions/bowsers-castle-1035-the-castle-comes-down.md</code>.</p><p>A Hammer Bro who guarded a room because Bowser told him to, and was still guarding it when the order was retracted too late to matter. The dragon asked him where Bowser was; he answered in Draconic that he was not the target, and then he told it his family history until it stopped being able to think.</p><p>Sir Frankfurt the fourteenth — or the fiftieth, depending on which part of the count he reaches first — and the tenth child of twenty-four. His father charged Mario and died before the third world was over; his mother died of grief a few days later; Bowser took in the surviving children. Bowser could be harsh, he told the dragon, but he had done right by them. The dented helm and the tabard with the 24 are his.</p><p>Built as a knight the party can be handed: two hammers, a reaction that protects the ally beside him, and the shell spin that got him out of the dragon's intake and off a fifty-foot wall. The record drops him 'into the unknown'; the sheet survives that fall at half damage. Roll it, and find out where he landed.</p><p><em>From the record:</em> the dragon's question, the family count, the shell striking the intake, the fall from the fifty-foot castle.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
